  "summary": "Validates the options parameter in the sendall RPC using strict type checking, rejecting any unrecognized keys. It also removes the unused solving_data option from sendall documentation and argument parsing, bringing option validation in line with RPCs like send and fundrawtransaction.",
  "problem": "sendall silently ignores unknown or misspelled option keys. A caller who typos an option like inputs as input will unintentionally spend all available wallet UTXOs instead of the specified subset, or inadvertently broadcast a transaction if psbt or add_to_wallet is misspelled.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'sendall silently ignores unknown keys in its options object, including misspelled ones: input instead of inputs spends all available UTXOs rather than the given ones, and a misspelled add_to_wallet or psbt can broadcast a transaction the caller asked not to broadcast.'",
    "Commit b517c3d915 notes that strict checking occurs before fee arguments are merged into options so that misspelled fee estimation options like estimate_mode are caught immediately."
  ],
